      "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
      "body": "Independent two-GPU RTX 5090 validation at head `747cbc8df6e81d52ba1b20060f8f9e04a4d4ff4e`: the upstream `TestTensorFragmentValues` passed ZeRO-1/2 × round-robin off/on (4/4). I added a setter check with round-robin enabled for ZeRO-1/2 × `parameter_alignment` off/on (4/4). It asserted a nonidentity parameter reorder and the actual per-parameter padding state. The full FP32 getter matched every named parameter before the write; after writing one parameter with `safe_set_full_fp32_param`, that parameter matched the replacement and every neighbor remained unchanged.\n\nThese runs used the PR's exact changed source and test over installed DeepSpeed 0.19.7. They cover DP=2 reads and writes with and without per-parameter padding; checkpoint round-trip and DP=4 remain untested here.\n",
